  "title": "San Antonio's Mayor Ron Nirenberg Blocks Drake After No Mention Of The City On Major Distribution",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":510696,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/GettyImages-1140654250-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-510696\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A new Drake album wouldn't make it without a Houston shoutout.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The rapper's new album \"Her Loss\", which is a collaborative project with 21 Savage, fell on Friday with 16 tracks and many authors and producers credited throughout. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>There is also a backlash for dubious words that many presume to target Megan Thee Stallion of Houston, but also because he forgot to mention San Antonio in the verse.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"I'm in love with Houston, Dallas, Austin,\" Drake said in the song \"Major Distribution. \"Tell your guys to hold off on the team.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>No mention of San Antonio, something the mayor of the city, Ron Nirenberg, didn't like.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"Last name, Ever. First name, Lamest,\" <a href=\"https://twitter.com/Ron_Nirenberg/status/1588600273781477377\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Nirenberg wrote on Twitter</a> with a screen of him blocking Drake. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/Ron_Nirenberg/status/1588600273781477377\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/Ron_Nirenberg/status/1588600273781477377\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->",
